WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.956
As Jo anticipated, her sisters were in awe of the Laurences' impressive estate.

2
00:00:05.957 --> 00:00:14.524
Even Mother paused to admire the elegant designs on the rugs as well as contemplate the splendid display of antiques in each room.

3
00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:19.507
"We are grateful for your hospitality," Mother thanked Mr. Laurence.

4
00:00:19.508 --> 00:00:29.451
The Marches were served an eight-course meal, of which they now enjoyed the final portion: a decadent chocolate cake with tea exported from India.

5
00:00:29.452 --> 00:00:39.062
Meg and Amy ate petite bites of the light, fluffy dessert, making sure not to show their teeth when they pulled the silver fork away from their mouth.

6
00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:45.662
With straight lady-like posture, they delicately patted the corners of their mouths after each nibble.

7
00:00:45.663 --> 00:00:51.897
Beth, who usually did not favor desserts, seemed to savor this particular one.

8
00:00:51.898 --> 00:01:02.032
Jo, unlike her more refined sisters, could not resist groaning in delight after each bite, causing Laurie to roll his eyes and make monkey faces at her.

9
00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:07.348
She returned the gesture, resulting in blasts of laughter from both parties.

10
00:01:07.349 --> 00:01:14.556
Shaking his head at Laurie but smiling, Mr. Laurence replied to Mother, "I am the one who is grateful.

11
00:01:14.557 --> 00:01:20.196
Friendship with your daughters has changed my grandson immensely."

12
00:01:20.197 --> 00:01:24.803
To Mother, Laurie had become the son she never had.

13
00:01:24.804 --> 00:01:30.272
"He is a sweet, dear boy. You must be proud of him," she said.

14
00:01:30.273 --> 00:01:38.943
Perhaps it was Mother's sincerity and kindness that moved Mr. Laurence to speak openly about his most devastating losses in life.

15
00:01:38.944 --> 00:01:44.726
"Theodore, or Laurie, as he likes to be called, reminds me of his father.

16
00:01:44.727 --> 00:01:53.370
They both have the same mischievous attitude, the same rebellious streak, and the same talent for the arts.

17
00:01:53.371 --> 00:02:00.396
I also had a little girl—the mildest, most adorable daughter parents could hope for.

18
00:02:00.397 --> 00:02:03.985
Your Beth reminds me of her so.

19
00:02:03.986 --> 00:02:13.443
My darling girl had a love for music, especially the piano, and she would play for my wife and me every evening.

20
00:02:13.444 --> 00:02:21.114
How I would look forward to returning home to the sounds of music coming from the conservatory.

21
00:02:21.115 --> 00:02:32.495
My son, after he became a young man, went against my wishes, and followed his heart to Italy where he fell in love with a beautiful young woman.

22
00:02:32.496 --> 00:02:44.969
She was also an artist. They traveled across Europe with their small child, Laurie, living like gypsies—no permanent home, no decent food or clothing.

23
00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.194
I was furious, of course, and refused to support them financially unless they returned here and lived like normal folks.

24
00:02:54.195 --> 00:03:00.955
Tragically, they died in an accident, leaving Laurie an orphan entrusted to my care."

25
00:03:00.956 --> 00:03:06.070
"You've raised a wonderful boy, Mr. Laurence," said Mother comfortingly.

26
00:03:06.071 --> 00:03:14.099
Mr. Laurence smiled sadly and said, "Although I may not say it to him enough, I am proud of my grandson."

27
00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:19.043
"What happened to your sweet daughter?" Mother gently inquired.

28
00:03:19.044 --> 00:03:22.759
Mr. Laurence's face was masked in pain.

29
00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:27.608
"She developed an illness when she was young and died of it."

30
00:03:27.609 --> 00:03:34.453
Mother remained silent as she looked at her girls, grateful that they were all in good health.

31
00:03:34.454 --> 00:03:38.031
"Grandfather?" Laurie broke the awkward silence.

32
00:03:38.032 --> 00:03:42.712
"Jo tells me that one of her sisters here has magic fingers.

33
00:03:42.713 --> 00:03:51.016
Apparently they glide effortlessly across the piano, creating the most beautiful melodies to the ears. Ouch!"

34
00:03:51.017 --> 00:03:59.053
Jo had just given Laurie a good strong kick to let him know how she felt about his unauthorized comment.

35
00:03:59.054 --> 00:04:07.210
As for Beth, she flushed pink as she slid lower into her chair and avoided eye contact with everyone.

36
00:04:07.211 --> 00:04:14.512
Mr. Laurence, already detecting Beth's shyness and reluctance to be in the spotlight, discreetly remarked,

37
00:04:14.513 --> 00:04:19.195
"I'm sure each young lady has a special talent of her own.

38
00:04:19.196 --> 00:04:24.024
Whether she chooses to show off that ability is her choice entirely.

39
00:04:24.025 --> 00:04:29.185
Now, I suggest we all go to the conservatory to relax."

40
00:04:29.186 --> 00:04:35.295
Everyone stood up and followed the master of the estate to his most beloved room.

41
00:04:35.296 --> 00:04:41.149
The conservatory room offered delights for everyone according to individual tastes.

42
00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:46.779
For Meg and Amy, a most exotic arrangement of flowers and plants greeted them.

43
00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:54.605
"What an exquisite piece of creation!" exclaimed Amy, bending down to smell a lavender flower.

44
00:04:54.606 --> 00:05:01.515
Meg and Amy strolled around the room, whispering, and nodding their heads in approval at the enchanting display.

45
00:05:01.516 --> 00:05:08.320
For Jo, a shelf full of books prompted her to squeal like a little girl.

46
00:05:08.321 --> 00:05:11.931
"Have you ever seen anything so glorious?"

47
00:05:11.932 --> 00:05:17.916
"What's so glorious about an old bookshelf with smelly books?" Laurie asked humorously.

48
00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:25.436
"It's what is inside them that makes them special!" said Jo as she ran her hand across the books' spines.

49
00:05:25.437 --> 00:05:30.630
However, it was Beth who felt the greatest pleasure of all.

50
00:05:30.631 --> 00:05:40.442
In one corner of the conservatory stood a stately grand piano, its lid rolled back as if to invite someone to touch its polished keys.

51
00:05:40.443 --> 00:05:50.342
As much as Beth's heart yearned to sit on the plush velvet stool and feel the ivory keys, she was too timid to act upon her desire.

52
00:05:50.343 --> 00:05:58.472
Her eyes never leaving the magical instrument that called to her, Beth inched away to the opposite side of the room.

53
00:05:58.473 --> 00:06:05.150
"This is my favorite room of the house," Mr. Laurence began in an unusually loud voice.

54
00:06:05.151 --> 00:06:10.032
"Unfortunately, during the day, nobody is around to enjoy it.

55
00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:14.767
Even the servants don't come in here unless I give them permission.

56
00:06:14.768 --> 00:06:20.236
Everything here, especially that piano, is longing for some company.

57
00:06:20.237 --> 00:06:24.966
Too bad no one can give it the proper attention it deserves."

58
00:06:24.967 --> 00:06:35.467
Mr. Laurence shook his head regrettably. Out of the corner of his eye, he caught sight of Beth moving out slowly from behind a large armchair.

59
00:06:35.468 --> 00:06:39.983
"Could I perhaps impose on the kindness of your family?"

60
00:06:39.984 --> 00:06:45.432
Mr. Laurence continued, pretending that he didn't notice Beth's obvious interest.

61
00:06:45.433 --> 00:06:53.791
"Of course, Mr. Laurence," replied Mother, already discerning what the wise old man was about to suggest.

62
00:06:53.792 --> 00:07:00.700
"Would one of you be so kind as to come here once a day to make sure everything is in order?

63
00:07:00.701 --> 00:07:06.269
And perhaps, play on the piano keys so they don't get stuck or dusty?"

64
00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:10.798
Mr. Laurence pleaded, his eyes lingering on Beth.

65
00:07:10.799 --> 00:07:16.131
"Would you allow one to play the piano?" Jo asked innocently.

66
00:07:16.132 --> 00:07:26.346
"You could do as you like," the old man replied with a wink, "because when the conservatory door is closed, no one can hear anything.

67
00:07:26.347 --> 00:07:32.930
No one will be around to watch or bother you in any way. You will be completely alone."

68
00:07:32.931 --> 00:07:45.247
"Well, I would love to help you, Mr. Laurence," Jo replied heroically, "but I am working during the day, as is Meg. And Amy attends school."

69
00:07:45.248 --> 00:07:52.649
"Maybe I could help, sir," Beth spoke so softly no one heard her at first.

70
00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:56.655
Then she repeated it in a slightly louder voice.

71
00:07:56.656 --> 00:08:01.010
"Oh, would you, Beth, dear? Are you sure?"

72
00:08:01.011 --> 00:08:07.657
Mr. Laurence intentionally walked over to the piano and tapped his fingers on the keys.

73
00:08:07.658 --> 00:08:11.818
"Look at the sly fox," Laurie muttered to Jo.

74
00:08:11.819 --> 00:08:22.606
Jo nudged Laurie in agreement but kept her focus on Beth, whose footsteps directed her to the piano, as if a strong magnetic force was pulling her.

75
00:08:22.607 --> 00:08:27.180
Her trembling fingers reached out and lightly tapped the piano.

76
00:08:27.181 --> 00:08:32.095
Then with more boldness, she brushed it much like stroking a cat.

77
00:08:32.096 --> 00:08:43.743
"It would be my pleasure, sir," Beth replied honestly, giving the old man a soft, grateful smile.

